1  \expnd0\expndtw0 1000 inches\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 beyond\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 track\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 of\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 car,\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 which\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 made\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 very\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 little\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 sense.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 There\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 is\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 a\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Preference\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Setting\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 which\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 lets\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 you\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 revert\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 back\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 to\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 the old \'93Kinematic\'94 method of calculating Roll Center, which was what we did before this new v2.4C.\expnd16\expndtw80  \expnd0\expndtw0 Figs A 6.50 and\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 A 6.51.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb2\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li446\ri29\sl244\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 De Dion rear suspension is now one of the Rear Suspension Types\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 you can choose from.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 The De Dion is somewhat\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 of a hybrid. It is like a independent rear suspension in that the differential or transaxle is mounted to the chasses, eliminating unsprung weight.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 But for suspension geometry, it is like a solid axle (live axle).\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 There is a beam that solidly connects the wheel spindles on right and left.\expnd16\expndtw80  \expnd0\expndtw0 Fig A 6.52.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow